-- Japan deep-dive content (English). A genuinely distinct shape for
-- this tracker: Japan has NO e-invoicing ISSUANCE mandate -- businesses
-- remain free to issue paper or PDF invoices. What's real and dated is
-- the Qualified Invoice System (適格請求書等保存方式, "Invoice System"),
-- a registration/documentation regime tied to consumption-tax input
-- credit, effective 1 October 2023 -- layered with JP PINT/Peppol, a
-- genuinely real but entirely VOLUNTARY government-endorsed electronic
-- standard led by the Digital Agency since 2021. No
-- deep_dive_penalty_rows here (matching the Finland/UK/New
-- Zealand/US precedent for countries with no real fine schedule): the
-- Qualified Invoice System's enforcement mechanism is economic (lost
-- input-tax-credit appeal for buyers), not a fine schedule, so it's
-- covered entirely in narrative penalties_related cards below.








